  "topic": "semantic_tokens",
  "subtopic": "references",
  "title": "Spelling forms",
  "summary": "Names keep their kinds in the less common ways C++ spells them",
  "prose": "An `auto` parameter is a keyword, not a template parameter; `new` behind\n`::` an operator; the class of a pointer to member a class; the left\noperand of an overloaded `=` is modified like a built-in one's; a member\ntemplate named after `template` is `unknown` until an instantiation.",
  "status": "supported",
  "issues": [
    "clangd#1390",
    "clangd#1627",
    "clangd#2235",
    "clangd#2547",
    "clangd#484"
  ],
  "files": [
